=== BLOCKED: platform-capability evidence (UI automation runner absent) ===
The only red step is the TeslaSync.App.UITests suite. Every one of its 147 tests aborts with:

  TeslaSync.App.UITests.Fixtures.UiAutomationUnavailableException : UI automation cannot run:
  WinAppDriver/Appium runner is absent: nothing is listening on http://127.0.0.1:4723/ and
  WinAppDriver.exe was not found at its standard install paths or on PATH.
    at WinAppDriverSession.EnsureReady() WinAppDriverSession.cs:line 75

This harness REQUIRES an out-of-process WinAppDriver/Appium UI-automation runner on
http://127.0.0.1:4723/ plus a deployed MSIX (AUMID) and an interactive desktop session. By the
suite's own design it FAILS rather than skips when that runner is absent (see
RunnerAvailability.Probe / WinAppDriverSession.EnsureReady: "the suite is never silently skipped").
None of that capability exists on this runner, so the UI-automation tests cannot execute. This block
is pre-existing, repo-wide, and orthogonal to CostSavingsPanel (the UITests exercise shell
navigation / packaging / manifests, not this surface).

